---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import PolicyArticle from '../components/PolicyArticle.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
import { policyLastUpdated } from '../data/policies';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Coaching Disclaimer | She Who Remembers"
  description="She Who Remembers offers coaching and educational work, not psychotherapy, medical care, legal advice, crisis support, or guaranteed outcomes."
>
  <Hero
    heading="Coaching Disclaimer"
    lede="Coaching and education. Not a substitute for care."
    surface="light"
    spacing="compact"
  >
    <p>
      This page states the scope of the work in plain language. It aligns with Private Guidance,
      the courses, the FAQ, Contact, and the book. It is a policy statement, not legal advice.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <PolicyArticle lastUpdated={policyLastUpdated}>
        <h2>What this work is</h2>
        <p>
          She Who Remembers offers coaching, educational material, reflection, and
          personal-development work. The aim is clearer self-contact, cleaner boundaries, and more
          honest choice. It is support for discernment. It is not a transfer of inner authority.
        </p>

        <h2>What this work is not</h2>
        <p>This work is not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>psychotherapy</li>
          <li>psychiatric care</li>
          <li>diagnosis</li>
          <li>treatment</li>
          <li>medical care</li>
          <li>legal advice</li>
          <li>crisis support</li>
          <li>emergency services</li>
          <li>prophecy</li>
          <li>spiritual authority transferred from you to a guide</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Coaching cannot treat trauma, depression, anxiety disorders, abuse, addiction, or medical
          conditions. When those need clinical, medical, legal, or crisis care, they still need
          that care.
        </p>

        <h2>Mental health and clinical care</h2>
        <p>
          Therapy and coaching may coexist when their jobs stay distinct. Therapy addresses what
          belongs in clinical care. This work addresses awareness, embodiment, boundaries,
          self-trust, and choice. It does not replace treatment, and it does not diagnose.
        </p>

        <h2>Medical care</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing on this website, in a course, or in a private session is medical advice,
          diagnosis, or medication guidance. Body-based language in this work is about attention
          and self-contact, not about treating a medical condition.
        </p>

        <h2>Legal advice</h2>
        <p>
          This work does not provide legal advice, legal strategy, or interpretation of your
          rights. Legal questions belong with a qualified professional in the place where you live.
        </p>

        <h2>Crisis and emergency support</h2>
        <p>
          This website, the contact form, a fit conversation, a course, and private guidance are
          not crisis services. They are not monitored as emergency support.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are in immediate danger, contact local emergency services or a trusted local
          resource. If you need urgent medical, psychiatric, or safety support, use the services
          built for that. This site does not publish a phone number in place of local help.
        </p>

        <h2>Relationship decisions</h2>
        <p>
          The work may support your patterns, communication, and limits. It will not tell you
          whether to stay in or leave a relationship. Those choices, if they come, belong to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          If there is coercion, violence, abuse, or an immediate safety risk, appropriate local
          emergency, professional, legal, medical, or trusted support is needed beyond the scope
          of this work.
        </p>

        <h2>Intuition and spiritual language</h2>
        <p>
          Intuition is treated as information to be discerned, not as infallible certainty.
          Spiritual language is optional. No belief system is required. The guide does not claim
          to know someone&apos;s inner truth better than they do.
        </p>

        <h2>Personal responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          You remain the one living the life. A guide may reflect a pattern, ask a harder
          question, or slow the pace. The decisions stay yours. Dependency is not the product.
        </p>

        <h2>Results and outcomes</h2>
        <p>
          This work does not promise healed relationships, trauma resolution, mental-health
          treatment, spiritual awakening, financial outcomes, or guaranteed transformation. Some
          people leave with more clarity. Some leave knowing this is not the right room. Both can
          be honest.
        </p>

        <h2>Referral and fit</h2>
        <p>
          Wanting support is not the same as this being the right container. A{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/book-a-conversation')}>fit conversation</TextLink> can help
          determine whether a course, private guidance, or another kind of support is the more
          honest next step. There is no prize for forcing a match.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Practical questions about the site can be sent through{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact</TextLink>. For coaching fit, use Book a
          Conversation when scheduling is active. For a fuller map of the work, see{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/private-guidance')}>Private Guidance</TextLink> and the{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/faq')}>FAQ</TextLink>.
        </p>
      </PolicyArticle>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If you want the map, not the exception list"
    primary={{ label: 'Private Guidance', href: withBase('/private-guidance') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'FAQ', href: withBase('/faq') }}
  >
    <p>The disclaimer names the edges. The work itself lives in the rooms those edges protect.</p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>
